    "media:imagetext": "Douglas DC-4-\nin 1935 Douglas began work on the DC-4, a\ntrunk route airplane. But by the time the air-\ncraft first flew in 1942, the U.S. was at war and\ntook over the DC-4 for military use. Many of\nthe 1,163 DC-4's built then, as well as 79 post-\nwar models, finally flew commercially after the\nwar. Length: 93'11\"\n• Wingspan: 117'6\". Cruis-\ning speed: 219 mph.\nSandy.\nBless your\nCopyright 1973 by Johns-Byrne Co., Chicago, III.\nPLACE\nSTAMP\nHERE\nGuill\nMockenso\nSpecial Offer\nPrints of this art available 9\" × 12\", ready to frame. Send $2.00 check or money order for each print to: Johns-Byrne Co., 161 W. Harrison, Chicago, III. 60605.\nPlease specify type of aircraft (DC-4 Tri-Tail). Complete list of other available aircraft prints will be sent to you with your order. Allow three weeks for delivery.",
